<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Super Heroes</title>
  <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  <script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('navbar') %>
  <main class="home">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="layout-container hero-layout">
        <div class="hero-content">
          <p class="badge">Welcome trainee</p>
          <h1>Super Heroes HQ</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Build your own hero compendium powered by the
            <a href="https://akabab.github.io/superhero-api/api/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Superhero API</a>.
            Explore hundreds of characters, drill down into detailed stats, and sharpen your web skills along the way.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn hero-cta" href="/catalog">Go to catalog</a>
            <span class="hero-note">Start by browsing the roster, then dive into individual profiles.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-highlight">
          <div class="highlight-card">
            <h3>700+</h3>
            <p>Heroes &amp; villains available via the API.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="highlight-card">
            <h3>JSON-first</h3>
            <p>Practice fetching and shaping data from REST endpoints.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Node &amp; Express</h3>
            <p>Wire an API-backed server that powers your catalog.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section">
      <div class="layout-container">
        <h2 class="section-title">What you&apos;ll build</h2>
        <div class="info-grid">
          <article class="info-card">
            <h3>Interactive catalog</h3>
            <p>
              Fetch the full hero list, implement fast filtering, and surface quick stats like publisher,
              alignment, and power score.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="info-card">
            <h3>Profile detail pages</h3>
            <p>
              Use dynamic routes to show biography, appearance, power stats, and connections for any selected hero.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="info-card">
            <h3>Server integration</h3>
            <p>
              Build a Node + Express backend that proxies the API, manages caching, and serves your front-end views.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section alt">
      <div class="layout-container">
        <h2 class="section-title">Learning goals</h2>
        <ul class="goals-list">
          <li>Consume third-party REST endpoints responsibly (pagination, errors, rate limits).</li>
          <li>Transform raw API payloads into polished UI components and visualizations.</li>
          <li>Structure an Express server with modular routes and reusable services.</li>
          <li>Deploy a maintainable codebase with clear separation of concerns.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section">
      <div class="layout-container">
        <h2 class="section-title">Project roadmap</h2>
        <ol class="roadmap">
          <li>
            <span class="step-title">Explore the API</span>
            <p>Review the endpoints, inspect sample responses, and list the data you need for catalog and profiles.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-title">Bootstrap the Express server</span>
            <p>Create routes for the catalog and hero detail pages, then wire a service that talks to the API.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-title">Design the UI</span>
            <p>Build reusable components for hero cards, stat bars, and info tabs with responsive layouts.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-title">Polish &amp; deploy</span>
            <p>Add loading states, error messaging, local caching, and ship your hero hub to production.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section alt">
      <div class="layout-container callout">
        <div class="callout-text">
          <h2 class="section-title">Superhero API quick facts</h2>
          <p>
            The API delivers rich data including biographies, power stats, alignment, work history, and group affiliations.
            Use these fields to craft meaningful comparisons, leaderboards, or even head-to-head matchups.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="callout-meta">
          <div>
            <span class="meta-label">Base URL</span>
            <a href="https://akabab.github.io/superhero-api/api/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://akabab.github.io/superhero-api/api/</a>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="meta-label">Rate limit</span>
            <span>Static JSON &mdash; great for local development without auth.</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="meta-label">Suggested endpoints</span>
            <span><code>/all.json</code>, <code>/id/{id}.json</code>, <code>/powerstats/{id}.json</code></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <%- include('footer') %>
</body>
</html>
